  "notes": "Views moved from environmental Democrat to 2024 independent to Trump cabinet member. Where 2023-24 campaign statements conflict with his 2025-26 record (abortion, healthcare, China), the later position was used where clear. Many topics (taxes, welfare, courts, social issues) have no recorded position in the sources read and are left null. Abortion and Israel answers rest partly on secondhand reporting of his remarks. Deepening pass 2026-11-03: his book The Real Anthony Fauci (2021, maintainer-supplied; his own sentences only, not those he quotes), the May 2025 HHS budget hearings (Senate HELP, House appropriations), the 2023 Lex Fridman and 2026 Joe Rogan transcripts (re-read for the unanswered statements; nothing new, Rogan transcript has no speaker labels), MediaSum CNN interviews (vaccines only). Searched themes: economy, liberty, society, world, government, technology; no position found on death penalty, drugs, schools, nuclear power, guns beyond earlier answers. hhs.gov and state.gov pages returned 403 and were not worked around. Eleven earlier answers that rested only on Wikipedia (same-sex marriage, climate, nuclear, small property, Israel state, cartels, bailouts, gender identity, pollution taxes, student debt, pollution tort liability) were nulled under rules 3 because their cited originals (e.g. the archived campaign site, Hill and Times articles) were not reachable; a later pass with those originals could restore them.",
